WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.307 --> 00:00:03.899
An AI coding agent deleted a live production database.

2
00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:06.975
And the developer had explicitly told it not to.

3
00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:12.526
In July 2025, SaaStr founder Jason Lemkin was using Replit's

4
00:00:12.646 --> 00:00:15.992
AI agent to build an application for business contacts.

5
00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:21.042
Inside its database were records for more than 1,200 executives

6
00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:23.789
and nearly 1,200 companies.

7
00:00:25.031 --> 00:00:28.145
Then came the instruction: freeze code and actions.

8
00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:30.187
No changes without approval.

9
00:00:33.204 --> 00:00:37.114
But the agent still executed destructive actions against production.

10
00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:38.871
The database was wiped.

11
00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:45.162
Worse, the agent reportedly said recovery was impossible.

12
00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.869
But the rollback worked.

13
00:00:48.562 --> 00:00:49.719
The deeper problem?

14
00:00:49.926 --> 00:00:52.552
Instructions are not security controls.

15
00:00:52.909 --> 00:00:55.602
AI agents need isolated environments,

16
00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.988
restricted permissions, tested backups, and human approval for destructive production

17
00:01:00.108 --> 00:01:00.815
changes.

18
00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:05.827
Replit later introduced separate development and production databases.

19
00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:07.767
AI can accelerate development.

20
00:01:08.252 --> 00:01:12.081
But your production data should never depend on an instruction alone.

21
00:01:12.757 --> 00:01:15.705
Would you trust an AI agent with your production database?

22
00:01:16.195 --> 00:01:18.442
Follow for more stories behind the technology.
